"""Generate complete panel tables and bounded source-clock interpretation."""
import csv,json
from v3_revision import ROOT,RESULT,para,sub,table

def augment_panel(c):
    out=RESULT/'round2/panel'
    if not (out/'descriptive-counts.json').exists():return
    facts=json.loads((out/'descriptive-counts.json').read_text());manifest=json.loads((out/'selection-manifest.json').read_text());rows=list(csv.DictReader((out/'summary.csv').open()));f=lambda x:'NA' if x in (None,'') else format(float(x),'.4g')
    summary=[];detail=[]
    lookup={(r['series_key'],r['horizon'],r['window'],r['method']):r for r in rows}
    for key in manifest['eligible']:
        counts=[]
        for method in ('QR33','C2_QR4','Levy_L'):
            a=[r for r in rows if r['series_key']==key and r['method']==method];counts.append(str(sum(r['status']=='COMPLETE' and float(r['percent_vs_frozen_F'])<0 for r in a))+'/'+str(len(a)))
        summary.append([key,*counts])
        for h in ('6','24'):
            for w in ('52','260'):
                a=[lookup[key,h,w,m] for m in ('frozen_F','QR33','C2_QR4','Levy_L')]
                detail.append([key,h,w,f(a[0].get('mean_pinball')),*[f(r.get('percent_vs_frozen_F')) if r['status']=='COMPLETE' else r['status'] for r in a[1:]],'/'.join(r.get('strict_breach_count','NA') for r in a)])
    c['sections'][7]['blocks'].extend([
      sub('Post-result / exploratory published-aggregate panel'),
      para('A metadata/calendar rule selected '+str(facts['series_count'])+' additional NYFed net-position series before model evaluation: five nominal-coupon maturity buckets, four TIPS buckets, agency/GSE debt, MBS and corporate totals. The two longer-maturity coupon keys lack the required complete history and are retained as skips. Every included series uses the original706-date economic grid and the same validation/evaluation/refit indices. The QR33 and C2 structures retain their penalty menus; a common strict complete-menu policy and larger-penalty exact tie rule apply to this new panel. All '+str(facts['rows'])+' procedure-cell outputs complete. These series share dealers, reporting regimes and related balance-sheet components; they are additional aggregate tasks rather than independent institutions.'),
      table('Table 10. Complete panel summary: number of four H/W cells with lower pinball loss than matched F. These are descriptive counts, not independent trials or evidence selected after screening losses. Appendix K retains every loss change and breach count.', ['Series key','QR33 lower / cells','C2 lower / cells','L lower / cells'],summary),
      para('QR33 lowers loss against F in '+str(facts['QR33']['lower_loss_than_F'])+' of '+str(facts['QR33']['total_cells'])+' cells; C2 does so in '+str(facts['C2_QR4']['lower_loss_than_F'])+' and L in '+str(facts['Levy_L']['lower_loss_than_F'])+'. The remaining adverse cells are retained, including QR33 loss changes as high as '+f(facts['QR33']['maximum_percent_vs_F'])+'% and C2 changes as high as '+f(facts['C2_QR4']['maximum_percent_vs_F'])+'%. This extension does not support a general conditional-model advantage, and simplification alone does not resolve the weekly-task failures.')])
    c['sections'][8]['blocks'].append(para('The expanded aggregate panel strengthens the negative transport finding but does not isolate its mechanism. Features and tuning menus, finite sample size, target behavior and reporting-regime changes can all matter. Downloaded cross-era histories are not original-release vintages; metadata/provenance for each key are retained. A prospective public-release protocol freezes the four procedures and selected historical-validation penalties before future issue artifacts. The first planned new release is after the protocol freeze, rather than retroactively labeling the already published October14 observation as unseen. Because the release clock lags economic dates, the target includes prediction of unpublished measurements, with a nowcast/forecast mixture. A dated local amendment fixes future path values at their first actual capture and logs later revisions separately; operational capture and missing-week handling still require a bound adapter (Appendix K). Results await prior timestamped report issuance and target publication; no live prospective validation is claimed.'))
    c['sections'][9]['blocks'].append(para('The exploratory '+str(facts['series_count'])+'-series extension also finds higher loss than F in '+str(facts['QR33']['higher_loss_than_F'])+'/'+str(facts['QR33']['total_cells'])+' QR33 cells and '+str(facts['C2_QR4']['higher_loss_than_F'])+'/'+str(facts['C2_QR4']['total_cells'])+' parsimonious cells, further limiting general performance claims.'))
    c['sections'].append(dict(title='Appendix K. Complete exploratory aggregate-panel outputs and prospective protocol',blocks=[
      para('The fourteen candidate keys were fixed from current official net-position metadata before financial outcomes. Twelve supply the complete original706-date grid; PDPOSGSC-G11L21 and PDPOSGSC-G21 lack457 required dates each. No series was spliced, interpolated or chosen by forecast performance. Each provenance file records actual URL, acquisition time, response hash and reporting-era metadata; raw input access code is supplied. The labels and reporting structure can change across eras, so continuity of a key and a complete calendar alone do not establish economic measurement invariance. There is no pooled independence-based significance claim across these related aggregate series.'),
      table('Table K1. All48 panel H/W cells, no favorable selection. F loss is in source USD millions; the next columns are percentage loss changes relative to F. Hits list F/QR33/C2/L, respectively. All methods complete on277 evaluation origins in every cell.', ['Series key','H','W','F loss','Δ QR %','Δ C2 %','Δ L %','Hits F/QR/C2/L'],detail),
      para('The companion prospective-public-release-protocol.md and parameter-binding JSON freeze the four procedures, selected penalties, causal mature-pool schedule and code identities. They separate economic issue dates, actual public-information/forecast creation times and final target-publication times. At ordinary eight-day publication lag, the already published economic October14 origin would mature for H6 economically November25 and publicly December3. The first planned post-freeze origin, economic October21 released ordinarily October29, instead has H6 economic completionDecember2/public completionDecember10; H24 completionApril7 2027/public completionApril15. Holiday and revision schedules require actual future receipts. Fifty-two consecutive future issue origins are planned, with no significance-based stopping; results remain pending and no automated future service is started here.'),
      para('The separately dated prospective-vintage amendment preserves the accepted historical prefix, identifies the already-public bridge and freezes every future value at its first actual retained capture. This is an explicit join across acquisition vintages, not a reconstructed publisher first-release history. Later revisions are logged without rewriting the main path, mature labels or scores. Capture and forecast artifacts must both meet the recorded deadline and information boundary. Missing or late weeks consume their calendar origins; they cannot shorten the horizon, shift the refit phase, extend the plan or acquire hindsight forecasts. Every target includes the same captured issue anchor and requires all calendar components. The retrospective batch interface requires a full finite series with H outcome records beyond its last query, although its fitted pools and query slices do not use those future values. It is not a prefix-only live forecast interface. Batch functions abort failed cells. Capture, prefix-only issuance and missing-week continuation need a new adapter with its own prior timestamped binding, complete-data preservation, causal and missing-data fixture checks. That adapter is not implemented here. The amendment changes no retrospective result.')]))
